\pard\plain\f0\fs22\plain\f1\fs22\lang1033\hich\f1\dbch\f1\loch\f1\cf2\fs22 Joshua Mandel is a 39 year-old male with a PMH of GERD who comes to clinic to establish care with new PCP/ annual wellness visit. \par 
\par 
Post -Concussion syndrome\par 
Chronic problem but not better after over 2 years. Has seen rehab medicine at UW and is working with OT and eye therapy. Discussed medication options including amitriptyline and BP medication. He has daily headaches and bad fatigue with staring at the 
screen. Unfortunately, his job requires a lot of screen time, so hard to avoid triggers that make symptoms worse. \par 
-- continue to work with OT/ eye therapy\par 
-- if not getting better, could consider TCA or topiramate \par 
\par 
HTN\par 
BP of 138/76 is consistent with Stage I HTN. Patient is interested in medication. He has tried dietary modification and feels like it hasn't been successful. \par 
-- labs: BMP ordered for baseline lytes and renal function\par 
-- start lisinopril 10 mg daily \par 
